      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not support the specific description that mood-congruent memory is a “pattern” where what someone remembers is influenced by their “current mood.” It only reports that patients’ memory showed a “mood-congruent memory effect.”",
        "The claim that it is “a typical feature of depression across different levels of severity” is only partially supported: the packet says it was typical and “regardless of the severity of depression,” but it does not explicitly frame this as “different levels of severity” in the definitional way the definition does."
